# Each entry below is a deliberate design choice for this project, not an
# oversight — reviewed individually rather than lowering the scan severity
# threshold to make them go away. AWS-0052 (ALB not dropping invalid
# headers) was a real, free fix and is NOT ignored — see
# modules/compute/main.tf's aws_lb.drop_invalid_header_fields.

# "Subnet associates public IP address" — the public subnets exist
# specifically to host an internet-facing ALB
# (config/flash-commerce.yaml: security.internet_facing: true), which
# requires a reachable public IP. Private subnets (compute/database/cache)
# do not set this and are correctly flagged clean.
AWS-0164

# "Load balancer is exposed publicly" — same reason as AWS-0164: this is an
# internet-facing workload by declared requirement, not an accident.
AWS-0053

# "Listener does not use HTTPS" — already documented in this file's parent
# README ("Known limitations"): no registered domain exists for this demo,
# so there is nothing to issue an ACM certificate for. HTTP-only is a
# conscious simplification, not a missed step.
AWS-0054

# "Security group rule allows unrestricted egress" — on the ALB (needs to
# reach targets/health-checks) and compute (needs ECR/CloudWatch/Secrets
# Manager/general outbound API access) security groups, broad egress is
# normal and matches the AWS-managed default security group behavior.
# Deliberately NOT narrowed on the database/cache security groups either:
# tightening RDS/ElastiCache egress without a live environment to verify
# against risks silently breaking AWS-managed maintenance operations
# (backups, option groups, engine updates) for an unverified security
# benefit, since inbound is already tightly scoped to the application
# tier's security group specifically.
AWS-0104

# "ECR repository tags are mutable" — deliberate: terraform/README.md's
# aura-control-plane workflow re-pushes the same `:latest` tag on every
# redeploy. Immutable tags would reject that push, breaking the documented
# redeploy flow for a demo control plane that has no versioned release
# process (yet).
AWS-0031
